# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / JavaScript / TypeScript (if tooling is added later)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Un-ignore the project's own `lib/` directory. The blanket Python rule
# above (`lib/`) is meant for Python packages (e.g., `mylib/__init__.py`),
# but this Next.js codebase uses `lib/` as the co-source directory for
# `design-tokens.ts` (story 1-5) and `canvas-modes.ts` (story 1-6).
# Story 1-5 fix: re-allow `lib/**/*` so the file is tracked.
# Surfaced in deferred-work.md 2026-09-24 (python-ecosystem ignore rule
# bleeding into a Next.js project; close with a `.gitignore` audit story).
!lib/
!lib/**/*

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
.yarn-error.log
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
.parcel-cache/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.vite/
.cache/
.turbo/
.vercel/
.netlify/
out/
coverage/
lib-cov/

